macOS: PE code reads and writes LastErrorValue at %gs:0x68, so keep that slot in step with the TEB.

What it fixes: on macOS the %gs base is the pthread thread block, and Wine mirrors only a few TEB
fields into it (Tib.Self, ThreadLocalStoragePointer, Peb; Highball's 0008/0009 add Tib.FiberData).
LastErrorValue (TEB+0x68) is not mirrored, and %gs:0x68 is pthread TSD slot 13, libc's gmtime key.
MSVC-built code reads GetLastError() straight from %gs:0x68: Unity's Mono runtime
(mono-2.0-bdwgc.dll) does so at 130 sites. Every failing Win32 call a Unity game inspects then sees
a pointer instead of the error: File.Delete on a missing save threw
"IOException: Unknown error (0x80f13910)" from gameModeSelection.startTheRun() and The Last Flame
never started a run (highball#99, "nothing happens when starting the game"). Same on Sikarugir's
Wine 10 and on this tree.

MEASURED (M1 Pro, macOS 27.0, 2026-09-20, spike/lasterr in the Highball repo): after DeleteFileW on
a missing file, GetLastError() = 2 and TEB->LastErrorValue = 2, while %gs:0x68 = 0x840040e0 (r5) /
0x13006070 (r11), a heap pointer.

How: Wine's PE DLLs use the inline GetLastError()/SetLastError() from include/winbase.h (the TEB
field through NtCurrentTeb(), not a call), so those inlines and ntdll's RtlGet/SetLastWin32Error read
and write %gs:0x68 on x86_64 PE builds (a no-op on Linux, where the slot is the TEB field). The unix
side swaps slot 13 at the same crossings 0009 uses for the QoS slot (syscall and
unix-call dispatchers in both directions, user-mode callbacks): entering PE code it saves the host
value in amd64_thread_data()->host_slot13 (0x348) and loads TEB->LastErrorValue; entering unix code
it writes PE's value back to the TEB and restores the host value. The PE side writes both the TEB
field and %gs:0x68 in RtlSetLastWin32Error, and RtlGetLastWin32Error / GetLastError read %gs:0x68,
so a value set by MSVC-built code directly is seen too. On Linux %gs:0x68 is the TEB field itself,
so the PE-side change is a no-op there; the unix-side change is under #ifdef __APPLE__.

Verification (2026-09-20, engine-wine-11.0-20260920T024505Z-0011b-lasterror-inline, M1 Pro,
macOS 27.0): lasterr.exe reads GetLastError, TEB->LastErrorValue and %gs:0x68 as 2/2/2 after the
missing-file delete and 1234 for all three after SetLastError; lasterr2.exe stays in step through
Sleep, CreateFile and CloseHandle (7/7/7). The Last Flame Prologue starts a run, plays its first
fight and saves, three launches, zero IOException lines; on r10 the same click threw. The first
build (ntdll only) still failed: Wine's own PE DLLs write the error through the winbase.h inline,
so without the inline change the TEB moved and %gs:0x68 did not.

Upstream status: not reported yet; a macOS-only Wine bug, WineHQ draft in the Highball repo
(private/drafts/winehq-lasterror-gs-slot.md) with lasterr.c as the reproducer.

